deadline (the caller was\n    /// cancelled). After the deadline, a late `Ok` is kept and any `Err` is `timedOut` (ADR 0046 §3.2).\n    fn settle(first: u32, body: Result<T, E>, deadline: Result<void, AsyncError>, timedOut: E) -> Result<T, E> {\n        if (first == 0) {\n            return body;\n        }\n        // No `Ok` payload is bound, so T may be void (bug B6: `Ok(value)` was invalid for Result<void, E>).\n        let reached = match (deadline) {\n            Ok() => true,\n            Err(_) => false,\n        };\n        let failed = match (body) {\n            Err(_) => true,\n            _ => false,\n        };\n        if (reached && failed) {\n            return Err(timedOut);\n        }\n        return body;\n    }\n}\n\n/// What `Async.all` returns once both children have: the first error in the order they returned, else `Ok`.\nstruct AsyncAllJoin<E> {\n    fn settle(first: u32, a: Result<void, E>, b: Result<void, E>) -> Result<void, E> {\n        if (first == 0) {\n            return AsyncAllJoin<E>.decide(a, b);\n        }\n        return AsyncAllJoin<E>.decide(b, a);\n    }\n\n    fn decide(early: Result<void, E>, late: Result<void, E>) -> Result<void, E> {\n        match (early) {\n            Err(e) => { return Err(e); }\n            Ok() => { return late; }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A one-shot wake-up from anywhere, to a task (ADR 0039): `await signal.wait()` parks the task until `signal.raise()`.\n/// `raise` has no effects, so an interrupt handler (`@context(irq)`) or another thread may call it, the way a driver\n/// tells the task waiting for its device. A raise before the wait is kept: the wait then returns at once. One task\n/// waits on a signal at a time.\n@noncopy // one signal, shared: a copy would never be raised\npublic struct AsyncSignal {\n    private words: [u64; 4]; // the runtime's record: raised, the waiting task, its executor, a raise in progress\n\n    /// A signal not raised.\n    public fn create() -> AsyncSignal => AsyncSignal { words: [0u64; 4] };\n\n    /// The same as create, in a static's initialiser (type-system.md §39",
